            "evidence": [
              "CountLenses (engine/review/app/lenses.go) validates the feature with review.CheckFeature before touching the store, and filters names with review.CheckResultName, so path traversal via feature or file name is refused; the test covers a traversal-style feature and asserts the store is not asked.",
              "Every stored result is read through judgedStored, the same decode and binding check used by verify and check; the judged refactor in engine/review/app/verify.go preserves behavior (same errors, same returned binding and result).",
              "CountLenses is read-only, returns a zero count with an error on any failure, and exposes no secrets or new input surface; no dependency changes are present.",
              "The .approval.json changes in skills/inception-pipeline and skills/role-chain are owner-approval hash updates carrying the approver labdrian; the skill contents they hash are not in this candidate, so they cannot be checked here, and nothing in the visible diff shows an authorization bypass.",
              "The overlay_dispatch_test.go and own-rdd.md changes are a test expectation and documentation only, with no security impact."
            ]
          }
