                "severity": "SUGGESTION",
                "claim": "CountLenses is added and tested at the app layer, but nothing in this candidate wires it to the actuals validator or a CLI verb, so S13 (validator refuses a mismatched review_lens_count) is not yet observable end to end. This matches T10 still being open in own-rdd.md, so it looks like an intentional first slice rather than a defect.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  "engine/review/app/lenses.go:30",
                  "odd/tasks/own-rdd.md:33"
                ]
              }
            ],
            "evidence": [
              "CountLenses refuses invalid features before touching the store, skips non-result names, and reads every result through judgedStored, so it holds files to the same rules as verify and check.",
              "judged keeps its signature and behavior after the judgedStored refactor, so existing callers are unaffected.",
              "lenses_test.go asserts the sums across launches, exclusion of verdict, exemption and other-feature files, zero count for an empty feature, and the zero count on every refusal path including a later read failure after a good result was counted.",
              "The overlay_dispatch_test.go change only updates the expected record usage string and carries no logic.",
              "The .approval.json files and odd/tasks/own-rdd.md are documentation and approval data, with no behavior to verify beyond what is shown."
            ]
